Default Statement in Java Switch CaseThe default case in a switch statement specifies the code to run if no other case matches. It can be placed at any position in the switch block but is commonly placed at the end.Example 1: Writing default in the middle of switch statements:
            Java

    import java.io.*;

class Geeks {
    public static void main (String[] args) {
        int i=2;
          switch(i){
          default:
            System.out.println("Default");
          case 1:
            System.out.println(1);
            break;
          case 2:
            System.out.println(2);
          case 3:
            System.out.println(3);

        }
    }
}

Output2
3
